{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>He who touches a corpse — he shall cleanse himself with it.</b> With the waters of the ashes of the cow, which purify one impure through a corpse. And from here emerged our custom of washing the hands after coming from the corpse, a reminder of the waters of the ashes of the cow, and it is also a reminder of the revival of the dead, when all the world will be careful regarding impurities; that is what the prophet said (Ezekiel 36:25): ״וזרקתי עליכם מים טהורים וטהרתם״. Also the plucking of grass is a reminder of this, for grass in the evening is plucked and withered and in the morning it sprouts anew, as it is written (Psalms 72:16): ״ויציצו מעיר כעשב הארץ״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:52.965815593Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}